# BINARY .asset overrides -- MUST stay last. The *.asset rule above marks every
# .asset as text with eol=lf, and LF normalisation rewrites 0D0A byte pairs inside
# a binary file, corrupting it. Unity writes these two in a binary format no matter
# what m_SerializationMode says. A later rule wins, so these must sit below it.
LightingData.asset               filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
ProjectSettings/XRSettings.asset -text
